Tangzhong
20 g Milk, 100 g Bread Flour
Cook over low heat, stirring constantly, until it thickens into a paste.
Let it cool before using.

18g Fresh yeast, 100g Milk, wake the yeast first
340 g Bread flour,
70g Sugar,
1 egg,
70g butter,
5g salt,
Tangzhong (all),
Dissolve the fresh yeast in warm milk first.
Mix all ingredients (add butter last) and knead until a smooth, homogeneous dough forms
(about 15–20 minutes).

Brown Sugar 150g, Cinnamon powder 1.5 tbsp,
Soft butter 70g.

Raise to double volumn (Either fridge overnight).
Roll the dough into a rectangle (around 30 x 40)

Spread soft butter over the dough then the cinnamon sugar. Roll it up (by long side).
Cut it by Dental floss. 

Set it into the baking plate (deep). Rise another hour.

Pour a little heavy cream over the rolls before baking for a softer, gooey texture.

Bake at 180 C for 20 minutes. 
